NavMesh in Unity - The NavMesh Agent (1/4)
A NavMesh agent is a component represented by a cylinder with a Radius and
Height. The agent will aim to keep a distance of Radius or greater between its
centre and surrounding obstacles and cannot pass under a ceiling lower than
the Height property.
The agent is able to query paths to the NavMesh, which are represented as
a sequence of waypoints connected by straight lines that denote the shortest
path. However, rather than follow this path perfectly, the agent will use more
realistic motion that incorporates acceleration and gradual turning, specified
by the Speed, Acceleration and Angular Speed properties).
As it moves around, an agent will avoid fixed obstacles in the scene as well
as other agents. The Obstacle Avoidance Type gives a hint to the navigation
system about how accurate the avoidance should be. The Avoidance Priority
determines how the agent will behave when it encounters another agent - the
agent with the larger priority number will avoid while the other will just follow
its normal path.
