NavMesh in Unity - The NavMesh Obstacle
A NavMesh Obstacle is a movable object that must be avoided by a NavMesh
agent (examples: doors that can be open, movable walls, etc). In order to mark
a game object as a NavMesh obstacle, you need to add a Nav Mesh Obstacle
component to the object.
The parameters Radius and Height specify the dimensions of the cylinder that
blocks the agent’s path.
There are two more parameters (Move Threshold and Carve) that are used
to let the agent calculate a different path if the obstacle is in the way to the
destination. If these are not used, the default behaviour is that the agent will
try to go through the path with the obstacle anyway.
